:A
THE SIG/M AND CPMUG COLLECTIONS

The default P: disk contains 310 SIG/M and 93 CPMUG volumes. These were
assembled by the CP/M user groups and circulated amongst enthusiasts.
They contain programming tools, source code, games, technical notes,
correspondence and programs written for particular makes of computer.

SIGM: and CPMUG: identify the two collections on the default P: disk.
Other mounted archives may have different names and contents.

:B
UNDERSTANDING LBR FILES

An LBR is a library containing a number of separate files. Individual
members may themselves be compressed. You can examine a library's
directory with LDIR and read its text members with LT without unpacking
the entire collection. YSEND downloads the library for local use.
There is no general caller facility for extracting members onto the
RCP/M disks.

:C
FINDING SUITABLE SOFTWARE

Look for abstracts, catalogs and instructions before downloading a
library. Not everything in a historical archive will run on every CP/M
machine. Some programs are written for a particular screen, disk
controller, terminal or operating-system revision. Read the author's
documentation and observe any copying or redistribution restrictions.
